{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/94203-true-abyssal-rust-and-cold-martyr-heart-in-the-bayou-of-endless-regret","id":94203,"title":"True Abyssal: Rust and Cold + Martyr Heart in the Bayou of Endless Regret","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-19T04:59:41-07:00","id":94203,"title":"True Abyssal: Rust and Cold + Martyr Heart in the Bayou of Endless Regret","content":"I have just binge-watched <i>True Detective</i> last week and I couldn't help thinking that Rustin Cohle would make a good Abyssal, most likely of the Daybreak Caste. He has had a near-death experience, he has a staunch nihilistic world-view and finally he has visions (Whispers) and other almost superhuman qualities (Charms). If I made a character based on him, I would probably throw in a background story in which he works as a taxcollector in order to justify his nickname, the Taxman.<br /> <br /> We only really have one official bayou in Creation, the Bayou of Endless Regret, and it just so happens to be a shadowland, so I guess that could be a stand-in for Louisiana as portrayed in <i>True Detective</i>. All we need now is an extended family of devil-worshippers reaching from the highest levels of government to the lowest levels of society. I guess that makes An-Teng qualify as a setting as well.<br /> <br /> The Yellow King would probably work best as an Infernal.<br /> <br /> But what about Marty Hart? He definitely has a dark side, but he is not quite Abyssal material, is he? Is he an asshole Zenith or Dawn? A Water Aspect? Or simply a Heroic Mortal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T06:17:41-07:00","id":94224,"title":"","content":"Hmm, based on some of his comments throughout the series, the fact that he is clearly setting himself against the darker elements of the setting, and especially the finale's final conversation, I can't really buy Rust as an Abyssal. Maybe as a renegade, but then he's not really fighting against his own nature as much as he's enduring what he sees to be the inherent nature of the universe. If I were to play him, I'd pin him closer to a disheartened Chosen of Endings who adopted a forced numbness after witnessing too many 'necessary' tragedies in Fate's design. We never see him MA, but he definitely views the world in a skewed perspective at times.<br /> <br /> Marty I definitely see as a DB of some kind. He's always portrayed as more of a competent foot soldier to Rust's otherworldly capabilities.<br /> <br /> I'd also say that the conspiracy itself is best modeled as an Akuma-DB cabal, although I like the idea that the Yellow King himself is an Infernal (even though, from what we saw in the series, the Yellow King of the show wasn't at the top of that particular food chain).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T09:31:34-07:00","id":94299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Side Item</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/94203-true-abyssal-rust-and-cold-martyr-heart-in-the-bayou-of-endless-regret?p=94224#post94224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, based on some of his comments throughout the series, the fact that he is clearly setting himself against the darker elements of the setting, and especially the finale's final conversation, I can't really buy Rust as an Abyssal. Maybe as a renegade, but then he's not really fighting against his own nature as much as he's enduring what he sees to be the inherent nature of the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like an Abyssal to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T13:05:27-07:00","id":94403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Side Item</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/94203-true-abyssal-rust-and-cold-martyr-heart-in-the-bayou-of-endless-regret?p=94224#post94224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, based on some of his comments throughout the series, the fact that he is clearly setting himself against the darker elements of the setting, and especially the finale's final conversation, I can't really buy Rust as an Abyssal. Maybe as a renegade, but then he's not really fighting against his own nature as much as he's enduring what he sees to be the inherent nature of the universe. If I were to play him, I'd pin him closer to a disheartened Chosen of Endings who adopted a forced numbness after witnessing too many 'necessary' tragedies in Fate's design. We never see him MA, but he definitely views the world in a skewed perspective at times.<br /> <br /> Marty I definitely see as a DB of some kind. He's always portrayed as more of a competent foot soldier to Rust's otherworldly capabilities.<br /> <br /> I'd also say that the conspiracy itself is best modeled as an Akuma-DB cabal, although I like the idea that the Yellow King himself is an Infernal (even though, from what we saw in the series, the Yellow King of the show wasn't at the top of that particular food chain).</div> </div> </div> </div>****Many spoilers****<br /> <br /> Rust definitely throws down some MA moves. First, he beats up a few mechanics to get a location for the whore colony. Later, he wreaks all kind of havoc during the drug-heist-turned-kidnapping with the biker gang. Aside from that, Investigation, Larceny, Stealth, Integrity, Resistance, and Awareness seem to be solidly part of his portfolio. On the subject of which Exaltation best suits him, Abyssal is really compelling due to his Whispers-esque hallucinations. Also, remember his compassionate advice to the woman who killed her kid? He matter-of-fact-ly tells her to kill herself as soon as possible. When Hart asks if it's possible to love two women, Cohle expresses doubt that love exists. He I'll have to dig up the lines that pointed this way, but I'm pretty sure he was planning to end his own life after solving the case, until his near-death experience gave him a new perspective. I'm not sure exactly how his, &quot;Nothing is ever over,&quot; claim fits with Abyssals or Sidereals. Overall though, an Abyssal who has discarded all the delusions that people use to assign meaning to life seems like a pretty solid match for Rust.<br /> <br /> I definitely agree that Marty is not operating in the same sphere as Rust, so DB or something else works fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T13:20:39-07:00","id":94411,"title":"","content":"Marty doesn't have the same &quot;power,&quot; so to speak - not the same insight, physical ability and manipulative skills - but he is just as valuable due to his connections, his social graces (he is a lousy manipulator but he actually takes the effort of making friends), to the fact that he can put on a public &quot;face&quot; for the two of them; without him, the case would have gone nowhere. In this he is a pretty close analogue to DBs in a mixed game - they lack the raw power, but they get tons of Background dots and can publicly advertise their Exalted nature much more easily, as well as counting on the support of the general state of the world going in their favor. <br /> <br /> It's a pretty clear representation of the difference between a character who puts dots in Abilities/Charms and one who puts dots in Backgrounds.<br /> <br /> But mostly they're World of Darkness characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T13:34:12-07:00","id":94428,"title":"","content":"While I agree he has a lot of Abyssal drapings and mutterings* , I think his overall ethos feels more Sidereal to me.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">His delivery of &quot;You should probably consider killing yourself&quot; is def how I picture an Abyssal using that You Can Be Less (or whatever it's name is) Charm.</span><br /> <br /> For one, while he is definitely nihilistic throughout most of the series, he always seemed to me to see it as a fact outside himself, not something he was engaged in/using. I admit there's an argument that most of his actions were fueled by his inner darkness but he always seemed to speak about it at a clinical remove. It also might be me bristling at automatically assigning all nihilistic/despondent characterization to Abyssals. Do Lunars not ponder the pointlessness and hopelessness of life sometimes? Can a Solar not question whether the concept of justice is real or just a lie agreed upon by society?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Heck, the tagline for the series <i>is</i> &quot;Darkness Becomes You&quot;</span><br /> <br /> My biggest reasoning for Siderealness, though, is Rust's continuing insistence on predetermination and the inability to escape his role in it. While I'm pretty sure the inherent metaphysics of Creation guarantee that time there is indeed not a flat circle, Rust treats things that happen as things that must happen. When he's pushed on how he can talk about meaninglessness of life and still go out and police, he points out that he's just fulfilling his role and couldn't hope to change it. His post-2002 actions also indicate Sidereal tendencies; basically, Something Wasn't Finished, and even though he ran away to Alaska for ten years he was still compelled to return and make sure that things were set right.<br /> <br /> My comment about MA was a bad reference to how SMA can do weird things to reality. I also &lt;SPOILER&gt; definitely agree that he was getting suicidal towards the end. My girlfriend thought he pulled the knife out of his gut at the end hoping it would speed up his demise. &lt;END SPOILER&gt;<br /> <br /> Man, this kind of stuff is fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T17:39:35-07:00","id":94571,"title":"","content":"SPOILERS SPOILERS SPOILERS SPOILERS SPOILERS<br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> I think the Yellow King was actually dead beforehand, and so not the serial killer. He doesn't seem like a king; I think it makes more sense for the Tuttle patriarch whose children were all involved to be the Yellow King, and I suspect the skull idol in Carcosa may have been him, or at least a representation of him. I think the show makes the most sense as an Abyssal and a DB teaming up despite the fact that they sort of hate each other to purge the demonic legacy of one corrupt Infernal patriarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1595-scatters-the-ashes","name":"Scatters-the-Ashes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T13:35:42-07:00","id":95922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Side Item</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/94203-true-abyssal-rust-and-cold-martyr-heart-in-the-bayou-of-endless-regret?p=94428#post94428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also might be me bristling at automatically assigning all nihilistic/despondent characterization to Abyssals. Do Lunars not ponder the pointlessness and hopelessness of life sometimes? Can a Solar not question whether the concept of justice is real or just a lie agreed upon by society?...My biggest reasoning for Siderealness, though, is Rust's continuing insistence on predetermination and the inability to escape his role in it. While I'm pretty sure the inherent metaphysics of Creation guarantee that time there is indeed not a flat circle, Rust treats things that happen as things that must happen. When he's pushed on how he can talk about meaninglessness of life and still go out and police, he points out that he's just fulfilling his role and couldn't hope to change it. His post-2002 actions also indicate Sidereal tendencies; basically, Something Wasn't Finished, and even though he ran away to Alaska for ten years he was still compelled to return and make sure that things were set right.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, his sense of, &quot;I'm a bad man in a meaningless, deluded world and I have a compulsion to punish worse men,&quot; feels almost stereotypically Abyssal. But splat doesn't equate to beliefs or personality, so yeah, that outlook could fit a Lunar who sees himself as a vicious beast hunting even more terrible beasts or a Solar who grimly carries out the tasks of justice though he feels abandoned by UCS or a Sidereal who sees Fate as a crushing burden that most everyone is afraid to perceive. You're totally right that we shouldn't assign a story or personality at that level to one type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}